{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790285486,"nonce":"U3m8r/cXup51Wzrj0KY/rgrBcLQ=","message":"Already done when this was migrated from the backlog. 0ced4eb (2026-08-20) replaced per-object line rounding with 16-byte quantum packing: allocate_kind and the TLAB bump round to 16, a small object never straddles a line, and the per-quantum objects table lets the marker find each allocation's start (a 16-24 byte vdynamic takes 32 bytes, not 128). 8a2da21 (2026-08-23) added line-level reclamation: the sweep hands out runs of unmarked lines in kept blocks, on by default (ASH_GC_RECYCLE=0 turns it off), made sound by per-object marking rather than per-line. The whole-suite interp flake that looked like a recycling bug was an interpreter cache (ca2f918).","files":null}]}